C9(a) Perturbations: the printed fluid equations (Eq. per2, l.249-251) contain (dP/drho)/(1 + w) and are singular at
  w = -1 (and c_a^2 = w - w'/(3H(1+w)) is too); CAMB's fluid module refuses w(a) that crosses -1 (checked: 'fluid dark energy model does not
  support w crossing -1'), and the printed posterior-mean trajectories cross; this does not mean every posterior draw crosses. The paper states neither PPF nor a patched module. We use PPF.
